  "title": "MySQL: Fix decoding of position for Binlog GTID",
  "description": "This is a small issue introduced in https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/9694 where `Send Binlog GTID` packets don't get dissected correctly if there is a `Binlog file name`.\n\nThis is not a common situation. This is when using something like `mysqlbinlog --read-from-remote-source=BINLOG-DUMP-GTIDS --stop-never -h 127.0.0.1 -u root -pxxxxx --ssl-mode=DISABLED binlog.000007` to fetch MySQL binlogs with `mysqlbinlog`. Usually this is only done with MySQL replication between two servers and a more common way to use `mysqlbinlog` is to let it read files from disk.\n\nExample capture (packet 28):\n[mysql_repl.pcapng](/uploads/40f1dc8017a75d74170899d78f3b43b0/mysql_repl.pcapng)\n\nWith this PR:\n![image](/uploads/c172640ab5d03388176e5d453900ba13/image.png)",
